.TH mouser-model-local 1  "mouser-model-local 1.4.4" 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
mouser\-model\-local \- The built\-in local model (gemma\-local): status, download, delete, url, dir
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmouser model local\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
The built\-in local model (gemma\-local): status, download, delete, url, dir
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
mouser\-model\-local\-status(1)
Engine, server, models dir and which weights are downloaded
.TP
mouser\-model\-local\-download(1)
Download weights (gemma\-4\-e2b 2.84 GB, gemma\-4\-e4b 4.59 GB); shows the size and asks first
.TP
mouser\-model\-local\-enable(1)
Use the built\-in local model: downloads (asks first) if needed and makes it the default. ID: gemma\-4\-e2b (default) or gemma\-4\-e4b; without one, the already\-downloaded model
.TP
mouser\-model\-local\-disable(1)
Stop offering the local model (downloads are kept)
.TP
mouser\-model\-local\-move(1)
Move downloaded weights to DIR (each checked against its SHA256 before the old copy is removed) and use DIR from now on
.TP
mouser\-model\-local\-delete(1)
Delete downloaded weights
.TP
mouser\-model\-local\-url(1)
Use an OpenAI/Anthropic\-compatible server instead of the built\-in engine
.TP
mouser\-model\-local\-dir(1)
Where model files go (`MOUSER_MODELS_DIR` overrides)
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBmouser\fR(1)
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH VERSION
v1.4.4
